WEBVTT

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:09.190
Hello?

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:10.810
Can you hear me?

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:16.200
Hello...

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:20.160
This is Mayuzumi.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:22.180
Eh? Dad?

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:25.240
"Dad?" I think you've
got the wrong number.

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:35.350
What was that about?

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:25.320
The old phone under the stairs?

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:26.640
Yeah.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:28.470
You know that's not possible.

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:32.530
Yeah. That phone doesn't work.

00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:36.080
Even before grandma was born,
no one's used the phone.

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:38.610
What? It hasn't been used that long?

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:41.240
It was used during your
great grandfather's time.

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:44.910
I don't think I was dreaming though...

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:47.790
It could happen.

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:48.410
Huh?

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:53.230
That phone actually rang once
when I was younger.

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:54.300
You're kidding.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:58.420
I am not kidding!
Was it in high school?

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:10.100
There's no way that
an unconnected phone can ring...

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:12.410
so maybe I was half asleep.

00:04:12.410 --> 00:04:14.100
Still... Huh?

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:16.280
Did you draw that, Mom?

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:21.190
I drew it when I was in college.
It's horrible.

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:23.160
Are you gonna throw it away too?

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:24.950
Well, it's pointless to keep it around.

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:26.720
All right, give it to me.

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:28.630
What? I guess you can have it...

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:29.910
Thanks!

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:33.600
Wow... This other stuff is cute too.

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:36.440
Whoa, what is this?
It's a fat bear. It's so cute!

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:37.670
Oh, just forget about that.

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:41.940
If we don't tidy this place up soon,
Miss Yukie will be here soon.

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:50.200
I'm terribly sorry to
bring boarders suddenly.

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:53.390
That's okay. We have
an extra room anyway.

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:54.700
Thank you so much.

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:57.630
And you're from
a non-profit organization?

00:04:57.630 --> 00:05:00.190
Yes, we're investigating wild birds.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:06.210
This is a great place, Tobi.
It even has an ocean view.

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:09.960
Yeah. Wanna go for a walk
once I'm finished here?

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:11.830
Sounds good.

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:13.830
Hello!

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:15.940
Didn't take you guys long.

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:18.010
You're already here, Yukie-chan.

00:05:18.010 --> 00:05:19.080
How ya doing, Atori?

00:05:19.850 --> 00:05:22.380
Wow, what a bright and cheerful room.

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:24.860
It was such a waste to have it
used as a storage room.

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:26.490
Right, Atori?

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:27.230
Yeah.

00:05:27.230 --> 00:05:30.020
Looks like Kaminogi's house
was the right choice.

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:31.860
Compared to Yukie-chan's apartment.

00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:33.920
Well, excuse me for
having a cramped apartment.

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:36.190
He's not here with you?

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:39.450
Karasu? He's probably out.

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:42.690
He should have lodged here with you too.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:46.780
We couldn't. It'd be too suspicious
to have an intense looking guy...

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:49.380
to pose as a wild bird researcher.

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:53.210
For sure. He's always got this scary
look on this face.

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:57.560
Well? Is this going to work out?

00:05:57.560 --> 00:06:00.890
Probably, although it'll
take a while to set up.

00:06:00.890 --> 00:06:02.820
Is it okay for you to be up and around?

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:09.520
What?

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:11.030
Nothing.

00:06:11.030 --> 00:06:13.970
I've brought the stuff!
Come on, guys. Help me out here!

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:16.070
Karasu! Where have you been?

00:06:16.070 --> 00:06:19.270
You just recovered, so you
shouldn't go outside too much yet.

00:06:19.570 --> 00:06:20.940
Haruka!

00:06:22.910 --> 00:06:24.280
Give me some of that barley tea.

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:27.300
Okay. You can pass it around.

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.280
Who, me?

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:31.050
Hurry up and pour it into cups!

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:32.990
Fine.

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:34.090
We have snacks too!

00:06:34.090 --> 00:06:36.560
Come on, Fujiwara. Help out already!

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:38.250
Yeah, yeah. All right, already!

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:43.900
Tobi-kun, is that good enough?

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:45.470
It's a real antique...

00:06:45.470 --> 00:06:48.560
but I'll try to
compensate with programs.

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:51.730
That happens to be
the latest model, y'know.

00:06:52.210 --> 00:06:53.530
Are you sure about this, Haruka?

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:55.280
About what?

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:56.770
You know...

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:01.150
They're floating!

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:02.650
That's impossible!

00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:04.170
Wh... What is this?

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:05.990
Super sorcery?!

00:07:05.990 --> 00:07:08.050
Move over Little Gray!

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:23.750
Okay, I'm in.

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:26.470
Wow, that's pretty!

00:07:26.470 --> 00:07:28.510
Super-impossible!

00:07:32.850 --> 00:07:34.820
What's Tobi doing?

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:36.620
There's something I want to look up.

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:38.520
Aren't you going to help out, Karasu?

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:40.190
Tobi's better at it.

00:07:40.190 --> 00:07:41.230
Oh.

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:46.530
Where ya going, Yuu?

00:07:46.530 --> 00:07:48.020
Bathroom.

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:57.180
Yuu...

00:07:57.180 --> 00:08:00.440
What's wrong? You're acting weird.

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:01.610
Let's go to Tokyo.

00:08:01.610 --> 00:08:02.210
What?

00:08:02.740 --> 00:08:05.850
I don't think we should
be anywhere near those guys.

00:08:05.850 --> 00:08:08.460
You don't want to get dragged into
any more weird stuff either, do you?

00:08:08.850 --> 00:08:11.470
I don't think running away will help.

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:16.160
That's not true! If we go to Tokyo,
your dad will be there, right?!

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:17.470
We can get him to help!

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:20.930
Actually, Dad's coming over
to visit this Saturday.

00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:21.960
Huh?

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:24.190
It's our quarterly date.

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:27.120
Oh, lucky you.

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:31.840
Besides, I'm the source of it all...

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:34.540
so I don't think it'll change things
no matter where I run to.

00:08:35.140 --> 00:08:37.650
So it's better to stay with Karasu.

00:08:37.650 --> 00:08:39.990
Is he that trustworthy?

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:42.220
Huh? Oh, really!

00:08:42.220 --> 00:08:44.120
How come you always talk that way?!

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:45.490
Oh, forget it!

00:08:45.490 --> 00:08:48.420
Just don't come crying to me
if something scary happens!

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:50.250
Wait, Yuu!

00:08:50.790 --> 00:08:52.260
What are you angry about?!

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:53.530
I'm not angry!

00:08:53.530 --> 00:08:54.930
Sure, you are!

00:08:54.930 --> 00:08:56.230
I'm not!

00:08:56.230 --> 00:08:57.260
You are!

00:08:57.900 --> 00:09:00.030
I told you, I'm not angry!!!

00:09:09.010 --> 00:09:10.850
See? You are angry.

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:12.840
I told you, I'm not angry!

00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:16.180
Yes, you are!

00:09:31.330 --> 00:09:32.370
Hello?

00:09:32.370 --> 00:09:34.640
Hello, this is Mayuzumi.

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:35.700
Dad?

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:38.800
"Dad?" I think you've
got the wrong number.

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:47.240
You're angry, aren't you?!

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:57.150
Where is this?

00:09:58.930 --> 00:10:00.180
Tokyo?!

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:02.160
Mom?

00:10:05.470 --> 00:10:07.260
This room...

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:10.770
This is the house I was born in.

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:27.020
Wh-What do you want?

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:28.990
We need to talk.

00:10:32.090 --> 00:10:32.690
Come.

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:34.720
I can't go up there, d'uh!

00:10:38.800 --> 00:10:40.220
Okay, fine.

00:10:40.970 --> 00:10:43.600
Haruka-chan, are you here?

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:45.900
I'm going now!

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:47.790
Oh, leaving so soon?

00:10:48.110 --> 00:10:50.510
Yes, I'll be back again tomorrow.

00:10:51.050 --> 00:10:52.500
Um, where's Haruka-chan?

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:56.570
Haruka? Maybe she went to
the store to get something.

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:05.580
Hello, this is Mayuzumi.

00:11:06.030 --> 00:11:09.520
"Dad?" I think you've
got the wrong number.

00:11:11.370 --> 00:11:12.860
Dad...

00:11:13.300 --> 00:11:15.100
You're angry, aren't you?!

00:11:15.100 --> 00:11:17.400
You're angry, aren't you?! Tell me!

00:11:18.170 --> 00:11:21.110
It's time. I'm going now.

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:30.370
What's your problem?
You don't even want to talk to me?

00:11:30.920 --> 00:11:33.380
Do you have nothing left to say?

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:36.390
Mom...

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:40.550
Why can't I find better
things to say? Dammit!

00:11:42.490 --> 00:11:44.090
Dad, wait!

00:11:51.740 --> 00:11:53.730
That's me when I was eight?

00:11:56.010 --> 00:12:00.310
Now I remember. Dad
didn't come home that night.

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:04.410
And they got divorced soon after.

00:12:25.870 --> 00:12:27.900
Hello, this is Mayuzumi.

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:30.120
"Dad?"

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:32.700
I think you've got the wrong number.

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:36.210
It's the same.

00:12:36.920 --> 00:12:38.890
It's that same moment in time again.

00:12:41.790 --> 00:12:42.500
This is super sorcery! Uber Technology!

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:44.590
I wonder where Karasu went off to?

00:12:44.590 --> 00:12:46.320
He's over there.

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:48.260
See? Over there.

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:53.230
What's he doing up there?

00:12:53.230 --> 00:12:55.830
Oh, look at Goto-kun! Getting physical!

00:12:56.100 --> 00:12:58.840
Wow, you don't get to see him
do that everyday.

00:12:59.070 --> 00:13:00.880
I'm going outside too.

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:03.480
Aw, wait, Atori!

00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:05.040
Wanna all go?

00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:06.840
Sure, why not?

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:09.600
Is this what you wanted?

00:13:10.320 --> 00:13:13.240
Can't you even climb a tree properly?

00:13:13.450 --> 00:13:15.620
What did you want to talk about?!

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:18.160
Haruka will continue to be
exposed to more danger.

00:13:18.160 --> 00:13:19.730
Yeah, that 's because you're with her.

00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:21.960
I swear I will protect her.

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:27.270
However, if some day
I am unable to do so...

00:13:27.270 --> 00:13:28.260
you will protect her.

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:30.610
What are you talking about!

00:13:30.610 --> 00:13:32.770
I can't do the stuff you can.

00:13:33.440 --> 00:13:34.750
Then become stronger.

00:13:35.180 --> 00:13:36.670
Get real!

00:13:39.380 --> 00:13:42.780
You must protect Haruka.

00:13:43.950 --> 00:13:45.760
You keep protecting her.

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:46.770
Why, you!

00:13:47.360 --> 00:13:49.260
Haruka likes you better!

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:53.280
Hey, are you jealous?

00:13:53.690 --> 00:13:55.690
Wh... What are you talking about?!

00:13:56.300 --> 00:13:58.030
Do you like her?

00:13:58.030 --> 00:14:00.520
D-Do not. I...

00:14:02.270 --> 00:14:04.860
I don't really...

00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:14.110
I thought she was a pain
in the beginning.

00:14:15.280 --> 00:14:16.270
But...

00:14:21.890 --> 00:14:23.520
Wow!

00:14:27.660 --> 00:14:30.030
But she had such a cute smile, that...

00:14:33.630 --> 00:14:35.230
I...

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:38.290
Was that the beginning?

00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:42.140
You protect her, Yuu.

00:14:43.310 --> 00:14:44.940
Be stronger.

00:14:48.020 --> 00:14:49.850
I "like" Haruka?

00:14:54.010 --> 00:14:56.320
Hello, this is Mayuzumi.

00:14:56.320 --> 00:14:57.810
"Dad?"

00:14:58.520 --> 00:15:00.560
I think you've got the wrong number.

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:03.190
You're angry, aren't you?

00:15:03.760 --> 00:15:05.630
You're angry, aren't you?! Tell me!

00:15:05.630 --> 00:15:07.790
It's time. I'm going now.

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:09.830
Wait, Dad!

00:15:17.140 --> 00:15:18.950
I'm back again.

00:15:18.950 --> 00:15:20.670
Hello, this is Mayuzumi.

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:24.610
"Dad?" I think you've
got the wrong number.

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:27.880
You're angry, aren't you?

00:15:28.460 --> 00:15:30.860
You're angry, aren't you?! Tell me!

00:15:30.860 --> 00:15:31.910
Dad!

00:15:34.930 --> 00:15:36.870
What can I say that will satisfy you?

00:15:37.670 --> 00:15:38.620
It changed!

00:15:40.030 --> 00:15:41.620
That's what I'd like to know.

00:15:43.400 --> 00:15:45.300
It's time. I'm going now.

00:15:46.140 --> 00:15:48.130
No! You can't go!

00:15:52.410 --> 00:15:54.400
Hello, this is Mayuzumi.

00:15:55.080 --> 00:15:58.110
"Dad?" I think you've
got the wrong number.

00:15:59.790 --> 00:16:04.130
You're angry, aren't you?
You're angry, aren't you?! Tell me!

00:16:04.990 --> 00:16:07.120
What can I say that will satisfy you?!

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:10.000
That's what I'd like to know.

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:11.700
You're always dissatisfied!

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:14.960
I gave up on my dream to be with you!

00:16:15.370 --> 00:16:16.970
It's not like I asked you to!

00:16:17.470 --> 00:16:19.800
No... That's not right.

00:16:20.170 --> 00:16:23.740
It's all my fault, isn't it?
That's what you want to say, isn't it?

00:16:23.740 --> 00:16:25.410
Oh, knock it off!

00:16:25.410 --> 00:16:28.780
It's all my fault, isn't it?!
You always...

00:16:28.780 --> 00:16:29.640
Enough!

00:16:29.640 --> 00:16:31.890
No... That's not right.

00:16:31.890 --> 00:16:34.790
Which past do you want to see?

00:16:35.560 --> 00:16:36.720
It's you.

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:41.000
As you wander through
the many dimensions of the past...

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:43.560
what are you in search of?

00:16:44.130 --> 00:16:47.590
No matter how hard you look,
your past will not change.

00:16:47.590 --> 00:16:49.040
That's not true.

00:16:51.770 --> 00:16:54.070
It's time. I'm going now.

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:59.410
You don't even want
to talk to me anymore?

00:17:04.150 --> 00:17:06.550
Hello, this is Mayuzumi.

00:17:06.550 --> 00:17:09.500
"Dad?" I think you've
got the wrong number.

00:17:14.400 --> 00:17:17.090
I wish I had never met you!

00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:19.100
Mom?

00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:22.850
And if I had the chance to do things over,
I would also choose a life where I wouldn't meet you!

00:17:23.470 --> 00:17:26.120
Why? But why?

00:17:26.120 --> 00:17:29.280
Your past cannot be changed.

00:17:29.280 --> 00:17:32.130
Will you continue
to search despite that?

00:17:32.750 --> 00:17:34.980
For how long do you plan to search?

00:17:35.720 --> 00:17:38.130
Until they patch things up.

00:17:38.130 --> 00:17:43.350
That past is not linked
to your dimension.

00:17:43.590 --> 00:17:44.560
But why?

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:48.850
This is ultimately no more than
an approximate dimension.

00:17:50.030 --> 00:17:51.930
I wish that I'd never tripped.

00:17:53.770 --> 00:17:56.630
If I hadn't tripped that day,
we would've never met!!!

00:17:57.100 --> 00:17:57.800
That day?

00:18:11.890 --> 00:18:13.620
Take care of tomorrow's report will ya.

00:18:13.940 --> 00:18:16.720
And in return, you take care of lunch!

00:18:16.720 --> 00:18:18.660
Yeesh. Okay, fine.

00:18:19.290 --> 00:18:20.020
See ya.

00:18:20.020 --> 00:18:20.720
Yeah!

00:18:21.630 --> 00:18:23.120
Dad...

00:18:29.100 --> 00:18:31.500
Ow...

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:34.500
Wow, these are good!

00:18:34.780 --> 00:18:35.730
Huh?

00:18:35.730 --> 00:18:37.470
Yeah, not bad.

00:18:40.470 --> 00:18:42.520
Hey, this is cute!

00:18:42.520 --> 00:18:43.970
Excuse me...

00:18:44.490 --> 00:18:45.690
Did you draw these?

00:18:45.690 --> 00:18:47.050
What? Yes.

00:18:47.050 --> 00:18:48.600
Can I look at them some more?

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:50.960
What? I guess so.

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:54.830
You know, these are really good.
The colors are really pretty.

00:18:54.830 --> 00:18:56.200
Excuse me...

00:18:56.200 --> 00:18:59.500
This one's awesome! What a cute puppy.

00:18:59.970 --> 00:19:01.490
That's actually a cat.

00:19:02.640 --> 00:19:04.370
That's true. I knew that.

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:06.330
Just kidding ya!

00:19:06.770 --> 00:19:07.780
Honestly...

00:19:07.780 --> 00:19:11.440
Whoa, this one's incredible!
The rendering style is great!

00:19:13.010 --> 00:19:14.110
Are you an art student?

00:19:14.110 --> 00:19:17.110
Yup! My major is traditional
Japanese painting. And yourself?

00:19:17.620 --> 00:19:19.850
Quantum data processing engineering.

00:19:19.850 --> 00:19:22.790
Wow, that sounds like
a difficult subject.

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:25.460
You don't really look like the type.

00:19:25.460 --> 00:19:27.160
Yeah, but I graduate this year.

00:19:27.160 --> 00:19:30.600
Oh, this one's cute too.
It is a tasmanian devil?

00:19:31.270 --> 00:19:34.100
It's a raccoon. A RAC-COON.

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:36.800
I know! I'm just kidding around!

00:19:36.800 --> 00:19:38.140
You...

00:19:44.810 --> 00:19:48.020
I'm sure you can find a past
where they had never...

00:19:48.020 --> 00:19:51.010
met in various other dimensions.

00:19:51.990 --> 00:19:54.650
However, doing so...

00:19:54.990 --> 00:19:57.620
would have no meaning for you at all.

00:19:58.430 --> 00:20:01.400
And that is because
they will never lead...

00:20:01.400 --> 00:20:04.420
to the dimension where you live.

00:20:05.270 --> 00:20:07.320
So you're saying
I can't change the past?

00:20:12.740 --> 00:20:14.310
I think that's okay.

00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:17.610
They really got along well back then.

00:20:31.230 --> 00:20:34.090
The dimension is getting
more unstable than I predicted.

00:20:35.230 --> 00:20:37.700
This feeling... It's similar.

00:20:37.700 --> 00:20:39.800
Can you tell? It's exactly
like it was before Shangri-la...

00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:42.380
began its invasion on La'cryma.

00:20:46.310 --> 00:20:48.650
We're all going out for
another walk tomorrow.

00:20:49.010 --> 00:20:50.980
Good for you, Atori.

00:20:50.980 --> 00:20:52.140
Yeah.

00:20:53.650 --> 00:20:56.850
What's wrong, Haruka?
You don't normally call like this.

00:20:56.850 --> 00:21:01.590
Don't tell me you're
planning to cancel our date?

00:21:01.590 --> 00:21:04.530
No, I just felt like
talking to you, that's all.

00:21:05.130 --> 00:21:08.560
Hey, Dad? Do you still love Mom?

00:21:08.560 --> 00:21:09.930
Why out of the blue?

00:21:09.930 --> 00:21:13.060
Answer me. It'll be our secret.

00:21:14.030 --> 00:21:15.140
I love her.

00:21:15.140 --> 00:21:16.740
Really?

00:21:16.740 --> 00:21:20.670
But I don't think your
mother would forgive me.

00:21:21.510 --> 00:21:23.010
Want me to ask her?

00:21:23.010 --> 00:21:25.450
You promised to keep it our secret.

00:21:25.450 --> 00:21:26.750
I'm sorry.

00:21:26.750 --> 00:21:30.020
Oh, yeah! Is there anywhere special
you'd like to go for our date?

00:21:30.020 --> 00:21:32.390
Let me see...
I'd like to ride a boat.

00:21:32.390 --> 00:21:35.690
The sight-seeing boat thing again?
We did that the last time.

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:37.890
Oh, right. Then the ropeway!

00:21:37.890 --> 00:21:40.880
Come on... Stop making fun
of your old man.

00:22:01.120 --> 00:22:03.550
Whew. I'm thirsty.

00:22:17.530 --> 00:22:18.770
Hello?

00:22:18.770 --> 00:22:20.960
Hello? Hello?!

00:22:22.940 --> 00:22:25.870
Excuse me, but this phone shouldn't
be working because it isn't hooked up...

00:22:25.870 --> 00:22:26.740
Mom?

00:22:27.170 --> 00:22:28.780
Hello?! Am I getting through?

00:22:28.780 --> 00:22:30.310
So, it was me.

00:22:30.310 --> 00:22:31.950
Mom, it's me!

00:22:31.950 --> 00:22:34.610
Huh? Who is it? Who's there?

00:22:37.180 --> 00:22:39.580
Hello, can you hear me?

00:22:41.360 --> 00:22:44.790
My self in some other dimension,
can you hear me?

00:22:47.340 --> 00:22:49.590
How am I?

00:22:51.030 --> 00:22:54.330
Please listen to me talk
to myself for a little while.

00:22:55.600 --> 00:22:59.100
When my dearest Yuu is feeling sad...

00:22:59.100 --> 00:23:00.740
please help him.

00:23:01.510 --> 00:23:04.380
That was something I could never...

00:24:42.280 --> 00:24:44.840
I'm dreaming again.

00:24:45.280 --> 00:24:47.080
That summer day's dream.

00:24:47.750 --> 00:24:51.410
Haruka, have you started
seeing ghosts again?

00:24:54.720 --> 00:24:57.410
You're wrong! Karasu
isn't an illusion!

00:25:01.060 --> 00:25:03.450
I would like to hear
about it in more detail.

00:25:04.100 --> 00:25:06.330
Next episode: Shangri-la.

00:25:07.170 --> 00:25:10.160
Can you see the other world?
